IMPORT prelude

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 (Singapore) -- who must compensate me, and what I keep or lose along the way.
--
-- SEAT: the employee injured at work (and, where the Act speaks of a death, the employee whose death it is: the
-- question is then asked on that employee's behalf).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3(1) "employee" with the Third Schedule, s 3(3) illegal contracts, s 7 (liability, the three
-- exclusions, the s 7(4) presumption), s 8 (deemed accidents), s 9 (accidents abroad), ss 10 and 12 (diseases),
-- s 13 (the principal), s 23(1) (no contracting out), s 24 and s 25(4) (insurance, and no deduction from my pay
-- for it), s 35(4) to (7) (telling my employer, and the claim deemed withdrawn), s 63(1) (suing my employer instead),
-- and s 34B(a) (which section applies to a platform worker instead).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 December 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/WICA2019.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 11 and s 11A (date of accident and apportionment for a disease), the Second Schedule's list of
-- occupations and diseases (whether my disease is listed for my occupation is a fact I state), Part 3A beyond the
-- s 34B(a) map, Part 3 beyond s 24 and s 25(4), the claims procedure in Part 4 beyond s 35, s 63(2) to (8),
-- s 64, appeals, offences other than s 25(4), and the machinery (Commissioner's appointments, regulation-making,
-- commencement, administration).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the injured employee, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 -- liability, from the employee's seat`

§§ `3 and Third Schedule -- am I an employee`

-- s 3(1): "employee" means an individual who has entered into or works under a contract of service with an employer
-- ... "but (b) does not include any class of individuals specified in the Third Schedule".
-- Third Schedule, "CLASSES OF INDIVIDUALS NOT COVERED": 1. "Any member of the Singapore Armed Forces." 2. "Any officer
-- of the Singapore Police Force, the Singapore Civil Defence Force, the Central Narcotics Bureau or the Singapore
-- Prisons Service." 3. "A domestic worker, being an individual employed in or in connection with the domestic
-- services of any private premises."
DECLARE `Third Schedule class` IS ONE OF
    `none of the Third Schedule classes`
    `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `an officer of the Police Force, Civil Defence Force, Central Narcotics Bureau or Prisons Service`
    `a domestic worker in private premises`

-- s 3(3): despite a contract of service that "was illegal at the time when the accident causing the injury happened,
-- the Commissioner or the court MAY, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, deal with the case ... as
-- if the claimant had at that time been working under a valid contract of service". A judgment handed to someone
-- else, so it is an input: the answer is "covered, if the Commissioner or the court so deals with my case".

§§ `7, 8 and 9 -- did my accident arise out of and in the course of my employment`

-- The facts of one accident, as I could state them. Every field is a fact; the Act's own terms are glossed beside them.
DECLARE `My accident` HAS
    -- s 3(1): "contract of service" is a term the Act borrows, so it is asked as a fact.
    `I work under a contract of service with the employer`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `my Third Schedule class`                                                      IS A `Third Schedule class`
    `the contract of service was illegal when the accident happened`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner or the court deals with my case as if the contract were valid` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1): "personal injury is caused to an employee by an accident"
    `I suffered personal injury caused by an accident`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1), s 7(4): "in the course of" my employment (while doing my work, at work, in working time)
    `the accident happened in the course of my employment`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(4): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
    `there is evidence that the accident did not arise out of my employment`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9
    `the accident happened outside Singapore`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am ordinarily resident in Singapore`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am employed by an employer in Singapore and required by my employment to work outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(1)
    `I was travelling as a passenger to or from my workplace with the employer's express or implied permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transport was operated by or for the employer, or under arrangements made with the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transport was operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(2)
    `the accident happened in or about my workplace`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was acting on an actual or supposed emergency at the workplace to rescue or protect a person, or to save property` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(3)
    `I was acting against a law, a regulation or my employer's orders, or without instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident would have arisen out of and in the course of my employment had I not been so acting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(a): "drug" is defined in s 7(3) by reference to the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973 and the Medicines Act 1975;
    -- whether it is proven is a finding, so it is a fact here.
    `it is proven my injury is directly attributable to my being under the influence of alcohol or a drug` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(b)
    `I injured myself deliberately, or deliberately aggravated an accidental injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(c)
    `I was injured in a fight or an assault`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I assaulted nobody, or only in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was breaking up or preventing the fight, or safeguarding life or property, or maintaining law and order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was doing so under my employer's instruction or with its express or implied consent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3(1) with the Third Schedule, and s 3(3).
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an employee covered by the Act` IF
        `the accident`'s `I work under a contract of service with the employer`
    AND `the accident`'s `my Third Schedule class` EQUALS `none of the Third Schedule classes`
    AND (    NOT `the accident`'s `the contract of service was illegal when the accident happened`
         OR  `the accident`'s `the Commissioner or the court deals with my case as if the contract were valid`)

-- s 9: "This Act extends to an accident that happens to an employee outside Singapore, where the employee is --
-- (a) ordinarily resident in Singapore; and (b) employed by an employer in Singapore but is required in the course of
-- the employee's employment to work outside Singapore."
-- That an accident abroad is OUTSIDE the Act unless s 9 extends it is an inference from "extends to"; the Act does
-- not say so in terms.
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act reach where my accident happened` IF
        NOT `the accident`'s `the accident happened outside Singapore`
    OR  (    `the accident`'s `I am ordinarily resident in Singapore`
         AND `the accident`'s `I am employed by an employer in Singapore and required by my employment to work outside Singapore`)

-- s 8(1): "travelling as a passenger by any means of transport to or from the employee's workplace" with permission,
-- where the transport "(i) is operated by or on behalf of the employer, or by some other person ... pursuant to
-- arrangements made with the employer; and (ii) is not operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my journey deemed part of my employment under section 8(1)` IF
        `the accident`'s `I was travelling as a passenger to or from my workplace with the employer's express or implied permission`
    AND `the accident`'s `the transport was operated by or for the employer, or under arrangements made with the employer`
    AND NOT `the accident`'s `the transport was operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service`

-- s 8(2): "(a) in or about the employee's workplace; and (b) while the employee is taking steps, on an actual or
-- supposed emergency at the workplace -- (i) to rescue or protect any person who is, or is thought to be or possibly
-- to be, injured or imperilled; or (ii) to avert or minimise damage to or loss of property."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my rescue deemed part of my employment under section 8(2)` IF
        `the accident`'s `the accident happened in or about my workplace`
    AND `the accident`'s `I was acting on an actual or supposed emergency at the workplace to rescue or protect a person, or to save property`

-- s 8(3): despite acting "(a) in contravention of any written law or other regulations ... or of any orders given by or
-- on behalf of the employer; or (b) without instructions from the employer", the accident is deemed to arise out of
-- and in the course of the employment if "(c) [it] would have been taken to have arisen out of and in the course of
-- the employee's employment, had the employee not been acting as mentioned ...; and (d) that act was done for the
-- purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disobedience forgiven under section 8(3)` IF
        `the accident`'s `I was acting against a law, a regulation or my employer's orders, or without instructions`
    AND `the accident`'s `the accident would have arisen out of and in the course of my employment had I not been so acting`
    AND `the accident`'s `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business`

-- s 7(4): "an accident arising in the course of an employee's employment is deemed, in the absence of evidence to the
-- contrary, to have arisen out of that employment."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my accident taken to arise out of and in the course of my employment` IF
        (    `the accident`'s `the accident happened in the course of my employment`
         AND NOT `the accident`'s `there is evidence that the accident did not arise out of my employment`)
    OR  `Is my journey deemed part of my employment under section 8(1)` `the accident`
    OR  `Is my rescue deemed part of my employment under section 8(2)` `the accident`
    OR  `Is my disobedience forgiven under section 8(3)` `the accident`

-- s 7(2)(c): no compensation for "any injury to an employee suffered in a fight or an assault on one or more persons
-- unless -- (i) the employee did not assault any other person in the fight or, if the employee did assault any
-- person, it was done in the exercise of the right of private defence ...; or (ii) the employee was, at the time when
-- the injury was suffered -- (A) breaking up or preventing the fight or assault; or (B) in the course of safeguarding
-- life or any property of any person or maintaining law and order, ... under any instruction or with the consent,
-- whether express or implied, of the employee's employer."
--
-- READING OF THE DEPOSIT. The deposited text prints the closing words "under any instruction or with the consent ...
-- of the employee's employer" on a line of their own labelled "(ii)", after (B). They are read here as qualifying
-- the whole of limb (ii), so that breaking up a fight is excused only on the employer's instruction or with its
-- consent. That the stray "(ii)" label is an extraction artefact is an inference, not checked against the PDF.
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the fight exclusion bar me` IF
        `the accident`'s `I was injured in a fight or an assault`
    AND NOT `the accident`'s `I assaulted nobody, or only in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A`
    AND NOT (    `the accident`'s `I was breaking up or preventing the fight, or safeguarding life or property, or maintaining law and order`
             AND `the accident`'s `I was doing so under my employer's instruction or with its express or implied consent`)

-- s 7(2): "An employer is not liable to pay compensation in respect of -- (a) ... alcohol or a drug; (b) deliberate
-- self-injury ...; or (c) ... a fight or an assault ..."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an exclusion in section 7(2) bar me` IF
        `the accident`'s `it is proven my injury is directly attributable to my being under the influence of alcohol or a drug`
    ..  `the accident`'s `I injured myself deliberately, or deliberately aggravated an accidental injury`
    OR  `Does the fight exclusion bar me` `the accident`

-- s 7(1): "Where personal injury is caused to an employee by an accident arising out of and in the course of the
-- employee's employment with an employer, that employer is liable to pay compensation under this Act."
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `My accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer pay me compensation` IF
        `Am I an employee covered by the Act` `the accident`
    ... `the accident`'s `I suffered personal injury caused by an accident`
    ... `Does the Act reach where my accident happened` `the accident`
    ... `Is my accident taken to arise out of and in the course of my employment` `the accident`
    AND NOT `Does an exclusion in section 7(2) bar me` `the accident`

§§ `10 and 12 -- is my disease a work injury`

-- s 10(1): where incapacity or death "results from a disease contracted in the circumstances mentioned in paragraph
-- (a), (b) or (c), compensation is payable as if the disease were a work injury":
--   (a) contracted "while employed in any occupation specified in the second column of the Second Schedule", an
--       "occupational disease specified for that occupation";
--   (b) contracted "after ceasing to be employed in" such an occupation, "within the limitation period for that disease"
--       (s 10(5): the Second Schedule's third-column period, "starting on the day after" I ceased in that occupation);
--   (c) contracted "on or after 1 June 2012", a disease "(i) ... not specified in the first column of the Second
--       Schedule; and (ii) ... directly attributable to an exposure to a chemical or biological agent and the exposure
--       arises out of and in the course of the employee's employment."
-- s 10(3): no compensation "(a)" for a scheduled disease where I am employed in the occupation, and contract the
-- disease, on or after 1 June 2012 and "the employee's incapacity commences or death happens, after the end of the
-- limitation period"; "(b)" for a limb (c) disease if incapacity commences or death happens "more than one year after
-- the employee ceases to be exposed to the chemical or biological agent".
-- s 10(4): s 10(3) does not apply to a death "preceded ... by any period of incapacity in respect of which
-- compensation is payable under subsection (1)".
-- s 12: otherwise "no compensation is payable to an employee in respect of any disease unless the disease is directly
-- attributable to a specific work injury."
--
-- The Second Schedule's list is NOT encoded: whether my disease is listed for my occupation, and whether I am within
-- its limitation period, are facts I state.
DECLARE `My disease` HAS
    `my incapacity or death resulted from the disease`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disease is listed in the Second Schedule for my occupation`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was employed in that occupation when I contracted it`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I contracted it after leaving that occupation but within its limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was employed in that occupation, and contracted it, on or after 1 June 2012`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `my incapacity began, or death happened, after the end of the limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I contracted it on or after 1 June 2012`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is directly attributable to a work exposure to a chemical or biological agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my incapacity began, or death happened, more than one year after the exposure ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this is a death preceded by compensable incapacity from the disease`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is directly attributable to a specific work injury`                          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disease` IS A `My disease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a limb of section 10(1) cover my disease` IF
        (    `the disease`'s `the disease is listed in the Second Schedule for my occupation`
         AND (    `the disease`'s `I was employed in that occupation when I contracted it`
              OR  `the disease`'s `I contracted it after leaving that occupation but within its limitation period`))
    OR  (    NOT `the disease`'s `the disease is listed in the Second Schedule for my occupation`
         AND `the disease`'s `I contracted it on or after 1 June 2012`
         AND `the disease`'s `it is directly attributable to a work exposure to a chemical or biological agent`)

GIVEN `the disease` IS A `My disease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 10(3) bar my claim for the disease` IF
        NOT `the disease`'s `this is a death preceded by compensable incapacity from the disease`
    AND (    (    `the disease`'s `the disease is listed in the Second Schedule for my occupation`
              AND `the disease`'s `I was employed in that occupation, and contracted it, on or after 1 June 2012`
              AND `the disease`'s `my incapacity began, or death happened, after the end of the limitation period`)
         OR  (    NOT `the disease`'s `the disease is listed in the Second Schedule for my occupation`
              AND `the disease`'s `my incapacity began, or death happened, more than one year after the exposure ceased`))

GIVEN `the disease` IS A `My disease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disease compensable as a work injury` IF
        `the disease`'s `my incapacity or death resulted from the disease`
    AND (    (    `Does a limb of section 10(1) cover my disease` `the disease`
              AND NOT `Does section 10(3) bar my claim for the disease` `the disease`)
         OR  `the disease`'s `it is directly attributable to a specific work injury`)

§§ `13 -- can the principal be made to pay me`

-- s 13(1): where a principal contracts, "in the course of or for the purpose of the principal's trade or business", with
-- a contractor "(a) for the execution by the contractor of the whole or any part of any work; or (b) for the supply of
-- labour to carry out any work, undertaken by the principal, the Commissioner MAY DIRECT the principal to fulfil the
-- obligations of the employer under this Act in relation to any employee of the contractor employed in the execution
-- of the work".
-- s 13(2): on a direction the principal is liable "as if that employee had been immediately employed by the principal,
-- except that the amount of compensation is to be calculated with reference to the earnings of the employee under the
-- contractor."
-- s 13(5): "This section applies only if the accident occurs at a place -- (a) where the principal has undertaken to
-- execute work; or (b) that is under the principal's control or management."
DECLARE `Principal answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commissioner has directed the principal to pay me, on my earnings under the contractor`
    `only if the Commissioner directs the principal to pay me`
    `no: section 13 does not reach the principal`

DECLARE `My principal facts` HAS
    `I am employed by a contractor in executing work for the principal`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principal contracted in the course of or for the purpose of its trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract was for executing the principal's work or supplying labour for it`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident happened where the principal undertook the work, or under its control or management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner has directed the principal under section 13(1)`                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My principal facts`
GIVETH A `Principal answer`
DECIDE `Can the principal be made to pay me` IS
    IF      `the facts`'s `I am employed by a contractor in executing work for the principal`
        AND `the facts`'s `the principal contracted in the course of or for the purpose of its trade or business`
        AND `the facts`'s `the contract was for executing the principal's work or supplying labour for it`
        AND `the facts`'s `the accident happened where the principal undertook the work, or under its control or management`
    THEN IF   `the facts`'s `the Commissioner has directed the principal under section 13(1)`
         THEN `yes: the Commissioner has directed the principal to pay me, on my earnings under the contractor`
         ELSE `only if the Commissioner directs the principal to pay me`
    ELSE `no: section 13 does not reach the principal`

§§ `23 -- can I sign my compensation away`

-- s 23(1): "Subject to sections 51 and 52(c), any contract or agreement by which an employee relinquishes any right of
-- compensation from the employer for work injury is void insofar as it purports to remove or reduce the liability of
-- any person to pay compensation under this Act." (ss 51 and 52(c) are the settlement routes under the Act; whether an
-- agreement went through them is a fact.)
GIVEN `the agreement gives up or reduces my compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is a settlement under section 51 or section 52(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement giving up compensation void` IF
        `the agreement gives up or reduces my compensation`
    AND NOT `the agreement is a settlement under section 51 or section 52(c)`

§§ `24 and 25(4) -- my employer's insurance, and my pay`

-- s 24(1): "Every employer must insure and maintain insurance under one or more approved employee insurance policies
-- with one or more designated employer's insurers against all liabilities that the employer may incur under this Act
-- in respect of every employee". s 24(2)(a): not "in respect of the excluded classes of employees prescribed". The
-- prescribed classes are subsidiary legislation, NOT deposited, so membership is a fact.
GIVEN `I am in a class of employees prescribed as excluded under section 24(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer insure against its liability to me` IF
    NOT `I am in a class of employees prescribed as excluded under section 24(2)(a)`

-- s 25(4): an employer who, "for the purpose of defraying or partly defraying the cost of insurance required under
-- section 24, makes any deduction from the earnings of an employee" commits an offence: "(a) ... a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both; or (b) if the person is a repeat
-- offender, ... a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both."
-- s 25(5): a repeat offender has an earlier conviction under s 25(4), s 34P(4) or s 35(1)(a) of the repealed Act.
GIVEN `my employer has an earlier conviction for such a deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my employer can be fined for deducting the insurance cost from my pay` IS
    IF `my employer has an earlier conviction for such a deduction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

§§ `35 -- telling my employer, and when my claim is deemed withdrawn`

-- s 35(4): "An employee must, as soon as possible after sustaining a work injury in an accident, notify the employer"
-- or the foreman, supervisor or person designated by the employer (s 35(2)(a)). "As soon as possible" fixes no number
-- of days; how many days it allows in my case is a judgment, so it is an input.
DECLARE `Actor under section 35` IS ONE OF `me, the injured employee`, `my employer`
DECLARE `Act under section 35` IS ONE OF `notify my employer, my supervisor or a person my employer designated`

GIVEN `the days that are as soon as possible in my case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor under section 35` `Act under section 35`
DECIDE `Must I tell my employer about my injury` IS
    PARTY  `me, the injured employee`
    MUST   `notify my employer, my supervisor or a person my employer designated`
    WITHIN `the days that are as soon as possible in my case`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `me, the injured employee`

-- s 35(1)(a): my claim "is deemed to be made ... when the employer first has notice of an accident".
-- s 35(5): it "is deemed to be withdrawn if the employer ... does not have notice of the claimant's accident at the end
-- of whichever period ... ends last: (a) one year after the date of the claimant's accident; (b) if the claimant dies
-- within the period mentioned in paragraph (a), one year after the date of the claimant's death; (c) any period ending
-- on a later date specified under subsection (6)."
-- s 35(6): the Commissioner may specify that later period "only if the Commissioner is satisfied that the delay was
-- caused by mistake, absence from Singapore or other reasonable cause"; s 35(7): never "if ... the delay was caused by
-- an action for damages being instituted by or on behalf of the claimant". The Commissioner's satisfaction is an input.
DECLARE `My notice facts` HAS
    `my employer had notice of my accident within one year after it`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I died within that year and my employer had notice within one year after my death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner, satisfied the delay had a reasonable cause, specified a later period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer had notice within that later period`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the delay was caused by my bringing an action for damages`                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My notice facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim deemed withdrawn` IF
    NOT (   `the facts`'s `my employer had notice of my accident within one year after it`
         .. `the facts`'s `I died within that year and my employer had notice within one year after my death`
         OR (    `the facts`'s `the Commissioner, satisfied the delay had a reasonable cause, specified a later period`
             AND NOT `the facts`'s `the delay was caused by my bringing an action for damages`
             AND `the facts`'s `my employer had notice within that later period`))

§§ `63(1) -- suing my employer instead`

-- s 63(1): "This Act does not confer any right to compensation on an employee in respect of the employee's injury if --
-- (a) an action in any court has been instituted by or on behalf of the employee for damages in respect of that injury
-- against his or her employer; or (b) damages have been recovered in any court in respect of the employee's injury
-- from his or her employer."
-- s 63(6), where a court action begun within a year fails but compensation would have been payable, is NOT encoded.
GIVEN `I have sued my employer for damages for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have recovered damages from my employer in court for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I lost my right to compensation by suing my employer` IF
        `I have sued my employer for damages for this injury`
    OR  `I have recovered damages from my employer in court for this injury`

§§ `34B(a) -- if I am a platform worker instead`

-- s 34B(a): Part 2 applies to a platform operator and platform worker as to an employer and employee, with "the
-- sections in the second column ... (called the applicable section) apply in lieu of the sections in the first column
-- (called the replaced section)". The replaced sections are 7, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17.
--
-- READING OF THE DEPOSIT. The deposited table prints the first row "(i) 7" with nothing beside it and "34N" alone
-- under the last row: the second column has slipped one line. Read against the headings of ss 34D to 34N in the same
-- deposit (34D "Platform operator's liability to compensate for work injury" answers s 7; 34F "deemed to arise out of
-- and in the course of" answers s 8; 34G diseases answers s 10; 34H date of accident answers s 11; 34I answers s 12;
-- 34K computation answers s 14; 34L assessment answers s 15; 34M medical treatment answers s 16; 34N temporary
-- incapacity answers s 17), the map is as below. 34E and 34J are not replacements.
DECLARE `Part 2 section` IS ONE OF
    `section 7`, `section 8`, `section 10`, `section 11`, `section 12`
    `section 14`, `section 15`, `section 16`, `section 17`
    `a Part 2 section that section 34B(a) does not replace`

GIVEN `the section` IS A `Part 2 section`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Which section applies to me as a platform worker in place of this one` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 7`  THEN "34D"
    WHEN `section 8`  THEN "34F"
    WHEN `section 10` THEN "34G"
    WHEN `section 11` THEN "34H"
    WHEN `section 12` THEN "34I"
    WHEN `section 14` THEN "34K"
    WHEN `section 15` THEN "34L"
    WHEN `section 16` THEN "34M"
    WHEN `section 17` THEN "34N"
    OTHERWISE "the same section, with the modifications in section 34B(b) and (c) where they apply"
